.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ckman-piv 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-piv \- Manage the PIV application
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-piv\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage the PIV application
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ckman\-piv\-info(1)
Display general status of the PIV application
.TP
ckman\-piv\-reset(1)
Reset the PIV application, deleting all keys, certificates and PINs
.TP
ckman\-piv\-access(1)
Manage PIV PIN, PUK and management key
.TP
ckman\-piv\-keys(1)
Manage PIV keys
.TP
ckman\-piv\-certificates(1)
Manage PIV certificates
.TP
ckman\-piv\-objects(1)
Read and write arbitrary PIV data objects
.TP
ckman\-piv\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
